-- title:
--   Finiteness of the two-chart Čech H¹ over ℤ_{(ℓ)}
-- statement:
--   Let $N \geq 1$ be a natural number and let $\ell$ be a prime. Write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} = \mathtt{ratLocalizedAt}\ \ell$ for the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and let $F$ be the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, in which $j =$ `jFull N` denotes the element given by the $q$-expansion `jq`. For a subset $S \subseteq F$, `chartAlg N ℓ S` is the subalgebra of $F$ consisting of all elements of $F$ that are integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra generated by $S$; thus `chartAlgFin N ℓ`, `chartAlgInf N ℓ` and `chartAlgMid N ℓ` are the integral closures in $F$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$, of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j^{-1}]$ and of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j, j^{-1}]$ respectively, and `inclFin N ℓ`, `inclInf N ℓ` are the resulting inclusions of the first two into the third. The assertion is that the quotient of `chartAlgMid N ℓ` by the supremum of the ranges of these two inclusions, regarded as $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-linear maps, is a finite (i.e. finitely generated) $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-module.
--
--   This is the Čech computation, for the two-chart cover by the $j$-finite and $j$-infinite charts, of the first cohomology of the structure sheaf of the integral model of the modular curve over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$: the quotient of the overlap ring by the sum of the two chart rings is a finitely generated $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-module, the finiteness statement that feeds the connectedness argument for the fibres of the model. It is used in [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.connectedSpace_pullback_igusaTo_specMap`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.connectedSpace_pullback_igusaTo_specMap), and it rests on the finite type assertion [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.finiteType_chartAlgFin_and_chartAlgInf`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.finiteType_chartAlgFin_and_chartAlgInf) for the two chart rings.
